  "statement": "None of the four CG 4-spaces is strictly supported on icosahedral edges. Their adjacent projections are nevertheless injective. The two odd channels (3\u22975 and 3'\u22975) project onto one and the same odd adjacent 4 (singular values sqrt((5\u00b12\u221a5)/10), ratio 2+\u221a5), and the two even channels (3\u22973' and Sym\u00b25) project onto one and the same even adjacent 4 (singular value 1/\u221a2). The map \u03a6 from the 4 inversion-allowed Yukawas to hopping pairing-currents therefore has rank 2 and kernel 2. The Hodge Noether vector current is a unique charge-0 ray and does not cut the pairing sector. Surviving dimension is 2: not a ray. The explicit counterexample pair is the odd (to 4_3) versus even (to 4_5) adjacent pairing-current. Handedness 3 vs 3' is not residual after hopping: those two Yukawas become parallel currents."
